<title>UK: UK says probing claims of illegal beef exports.</title>
<headline>UK says probing claims of illegal beef exports.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain is aware of allegations that hundreds of tonnes of its beef has been illegally exported and had been investigating them even before the European Commission revealed them on Thursday, an Agriculture Ministry spokewoman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Action will be taken if the allegations are proved to be correct,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>At a news conference in Brussels earlier, a Commission spokesman said 700 tonnes of beef had been sent to the Netherlands via Brussels and some 900 tonnes had probably been exported to Russia and Egypt.</p>
<p>The European Union has banned British beef exports worldwide because of the mad cow disease scare.</p>
</text>
